From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:51:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: declare MSL temporaries without a dead store

MSL has no SSA form, so nir_to_msl declares every value at function scope
and assigns it where its instruction sits.  The declaration also carried an
initializer, so each temporary was written twice: once with a zero that no
path can observe, and once with the value.  The shader leaves SSA form with
phi webs only, so a temporary is always assigned by its own instruction
before any use can read it, and widening its C scope to the whole function
only matches the dominance the definition already has.  Registers are the
exception - a phi web can be read on a path that has not written it - so
those keep their zero.

The dead store is not merely wasted text.  Metal's out-of-process compiler
degrades sharply in the number of entry-block stores: the compute shader
that KHR-Single-GL46.arrays_of_arrays_gl.SubroutineFunctionCalls2 builds
for dmat4 declares 79822 temporaries after the GL front end emulates fp64
in software, and Metal answers the 8.4 MB source with
XPC_ERROR_CONNECTION_INTERRUPTED after 938 s and several retries.  Dropping
the 79822 dead stores - 9% of the source - compiles the same shader in
28 s.  A library that fails to build leaves the draw with no pipeline, so
the test read back zeroes and reported an invalid result.

(cherry picked from commit 41d93b279ff8d8dd9f776f13b386f4add2755107)
(cherry picked from commit df9f8eb5bd5e2f1fa1e086298577886fa1c4fc84)
